            <ArticleTitle>Total hip arthroplasty in Klippel-Trenaunay syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>W6-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1308/147870808X303182</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Klippel-Trenaunay syndrome patients often suffer degenerative joint disease at an early age. Performing arthroplasty in these patients is particularly difficult for a number of reasons. In this case report, we describe the second reported case of total hip replacement in Klippel-Trenaunay syndrome, using novel techniques to surmount the problems faced in this challenging condition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
